Hence $f(n) = M^\ast$. Moreover, by minimality of $M^\ast$:
$$\operatorname{sq}(n) \notin \operatorname{span}\{\operatorname{sq}(a) : n < a \le M^\ast - 1\}, \tag{$\ast\ast$}$$
and since $\operatorname{sq}(n) \in \operatorname{span}\{\operatorname{sq}(a) : n < a \le M^\ast\}$, the element $\operatorname{sq}(M^\ast)$ must be essential, meaning:
$$\operatorname{sq}(n) \oplus \operatorname{sq}(M^\ast) \in \operatorname{span}\{\operatorname{sq}(a) : n < a \le M^\ast - 1\}. \tag{$\ast\ast\ast$}$$

